00:36:37.820 --> 00:36:39.890
That was probably
about nine months ago.

00:36:39.890 --> 00:36:41.360
I'm particularly proud of this.

00:36:41.360 --> 00:36:44.280
We're not in the Gartner
Magic Quadrant at the moment,

00:36:44.280 --> 00:36:47.720
but our customers went and
nominated us for this award.

00:36:47.720 --> 00:36:50.870
They said things like,
we like Google EMM

00:36:50.870 --> 00:36:52.770
because it's simple
and easy to use.

00:36:52.770 --> 00:36:54.812
And those are the things
that we're trying to do.

00:36:54.812 --> 00:36:58.230
So, that makes me very happy.

00:36:58.230 --> 00:37:00.410
Hopefully, you take away
one thing from this talk.

00:37:00.410 --> 00:37:02.560
I think device management
is very important.

00:37:02.560 --> 00:37:04.710
I'm pretty biased
about that because I'm

00:37:04.710 --> 00:37:07.120
the product lead for device
management at Google.

00:37:07.120 --> 00:37:11.455
But I think if you're allowing
access to your enterprise data

00:37:11.455 --> 00:37:13.830
out in the wild, you really
need to make sure that you've

00:37:13.830 --> 00:37:16.020
locked that down in some way.

00:37:16.020 --> 00:37:20.560
So you can get device
management anywhere.

00:37:20.560 --> 00:37:22.235
It doesn't have to be with us.

00:37:22.235 --> 00:37:23.610
What I want to
make sure you know

00:37:23.610 --> 00:37:25.090
is it doesn't have
to be difficult.

00:37:25.090 --> 00:37:28.427
So if you already are a G Suite
user, if you're already a G

00:37:28.427 --> 00:37:30.510
Suite customer, if you're
already a Cloud Identity

00:37:30.510 --> 00:37:34.530
customer, you can get it
from us at no extra charge.

00:37:34.530 --> 00:37:37.080
So, you know, you don't
have to get it from us,

00:37:37.080 --> 00:37:38.400
but get it somewhere.

00:37:38.400 --> 00:37:39.820
That's what I'm trying to say.

00:37:39.820 --> 00:37:43.630
So, if you'd like to learn
more about what we're doing,

00:37:43.630 --> 00:37:46.945
you can go to
cloud.google.com/identity.

00:37:46.945 --> 00:37:48.570
And if you're
interested, specifically,

00:37:48.570 --> 00:37:50.310
in the BeyondCorp
